# Who owns this repository, and who GitHub asks to review a change to it.
#
# One owner, one line. Finer-grained rules would be fiction here: every path
# has the same owner, and a list that pretends otherwise ages into a claim
# nobody checks.
#
# What this file does: a pull request opened by anyone else automatically
# requests a review from the owner, so an outside contribution does not sit
# unnoticed because nobody was asked.
#
# What it does not do: GitHub never requests a review from the person who
# opened the pull request, and nobody can approve their own. A branch rule that
# demands a code-owner approval would therefore demand one, on every change the
# owner writes, from somebody who does not exist - and no pull request could
# ever be merged. That rule stays off while this file names one person.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style patterns, except that a pattern may not start with
# `#`, `!` does not negate, and `[ ]` character ranges do not work.

